@model OCRPrototype.Models.OcrUploadViewModel
@using System.Text.Json
@using OCRPrototype.Models
@{ ViewData["Title"] = "Egyptian ID front OCR"; }
<div class="container py-4" style="max-width: 800px">
    <h1 class="h3">Egyptian ID front OCR</h1>
    <p>Upload an upright JPEG or PNG, cropped to the card edges. Use even lighting and keep every field visible.</p>
    <form asp-action="Index" method="post" enctype="multipart/form-data">
        @Html.AntiForgeryToken()
        <input asp-for="IdImage" type="file" accept="image/jpeg,image/png" class="form-control mb-3" required />
        <div asp-validation-summary="All" class="text-danger"></div>
        <button class="btn btn-primary" type="submit">Extract front</button>
    </form>
    @if (Model.Result is { } result)
    {
        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">@(result.IsSuccess ? "Extracted fields" : "Needs review")</h2>
        @if (result.ErrorMessage is { } error) { <p class="text-danger">@error</p> }
        @if (result.Data is { } data)
        {
            <dl>
                <dt>Full name</dt><dd dir="auto">@data.FullName</dd>
                <dt>Address</dt><dd dir="auto">@data.Address</dd>
                <dt>National ID</dt><dd dir="ltr">@data.NationalId</dd>
                <dt>Card ID</dt><dd dir="ltr">@data.CardId</dd>
                <dt>Date of birth (from national ID)</dt><dd>@data.DateOfBirth?.ToString("yyyy-MM-dd")</dd>
            </dl>
        }
        <pre class="bg-light p-3" dir="ltr">@JsonSerializer.Serialize(result, OcrJsonContext.Default.OcrExtractionResult)</pre>
    }
</div>
